            <ArticleTitle>On the competition between weak O-H···F and C-H···F hydrogen bonds, in cooperation with C-H···O contacts, in the difluoromethane - tert-butyl alcohol cluster.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>90-95</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jms.2017.04.001</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The 1:1 complex of tert-butyl alcohol with difluoromethane has been characterized by means of a joint experimental-computational investigation. Its rotational spectrum has been recorded by using a pulsed-jet Fourier-Transform microwave spectrometer. The experimental work has been guided and supported by accurate quantum-chemical calculations. In particular, the computed potential energy landscape pointed out the formation of three stable isomers. However, the very low interconversion barriers explain why only one isomer, showing one O-H···F and two C-H···O weak hydrogen bonds, has been experimentally characterized. The effect of the H → tert-butyl- group substitution has been analyzed from the comparison to the difluoromethane-water adduct.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
